tasks.condition:
Say:
Скажи:
1) what singers / songs are popular with your friends;
2) what sportsmen and sportswomen are popular with your friends;
3) what games are popular with schoolchildren;
4) what places are popular with visitors to your city / town;
5) what books, magazines are popular with pupils of your class.

After doing ex.1–3 choose three pupils who know the UK and its people well. Let them answer your and your classmates’ ques-tions. You want to know:
После выполнения примеров 1–3 выбери трех учеников, которые хорошо знают Великобританию и ее жителей. Пусть они ответят на твои  вопросы и вопросы твоих одноклассников. Ты хочешь знать:
1) what part of London he likes most of all and why;
2) what the Tower of London used to be and what it is now;
3) why Londoners keep black ravens in the Tower of London;
4) what place in London is believed to be its geographical centre;
5) where the Queen lived;
6) why the clock on one of the towers of the Houses of Parliament is called Big Ben;
7) how often people can hear the sound of Big Ben;
8) if tourists can get into the Houses of Parliament and watch the sessions of Parliament;
9) what the difference between the House of Lords and the House of Commons is;
10) what Poets’ Corner is and in what London church it can be found;
11) why British people speak so much about the weather;
12) in what way the British people differ from people on the continent.

You are going to have a quiz on the topic “Britain. Then and Now”. Get ready to give the most important information on these:
У вас будет викторина на тему «Британия. Тогда и сейчас». Приготовьтесь предоставить наиболее важную информацию по этим вопросам:
1) the geographical position of the UK;
2) the political system in the UK (the Queen/King and Parliament);
3) the Romans in Britain;
4) the Great Fire of London;
5) London, the capital and the heart of Great Britain;
6) London’s places of interest;
7) British traditions and holidays.

Name them.
Назови их.
1) 3–5 things that can be: a) attractive; b) exciting;
2) 3–5 universities that you know;
3) 3–5 things that can: a) excite people; b) attract people; c) con-nect people or things;
4) 3 things that can be in the shape of: a) a heart; b) a square; c) an oval;
5) 5 things that you really admire.

tasks.solution:
1)
3–5 things that can be: a) attractive — people, house, sunset; b) exciting — ride, adventure, concert;
2)
3–5 universities that you know: Oxford, Cambridge, Harvard, Stanford University, Lomonosov Moscow State University;
3)
3–5 things that can: a) excite people — a sport event, a party, movie release; b) attract people — well-known restaurant, concert, festival; c) connect people or things — a bridge, Internet, roads;
4)
3 things that can be in shape of:  a) a heart — a box of chocolate, a letter, jewelry; b) a square — a box, a paper, a chessboard; c) an oval — an egg, mirror, a ball;
5)
5 things that you really admire: resilience in people, acts of kindness, artistic creativity, scientific discoveries, nature’s beauty.
Перевод:
1)
3–5 вещей, которые могут быть: а) привлекательными — люди, дом, закат солнца; b) захватывающими — поездка, приключение, концерт;
2)
3–5 известных вам университетов: Оксфорд, Кембридж, Гарвард, Стэнфордский университет, Московский государственный университет имени М.В. Ломоносова;
3)
3–5 вещей, которые могут: а) взволновать людей — спортивное мероприятие, вечеринка, показ фильма; b) привлечь людей — известный ресторан, концерт, фестиваль; c) соединить людей или объекты — мост, интернет, дороги.;
4)
3 предмета, которые могут быть в форме: а) сердца — коробки шоколада, письма, украшения; b) квадрата — коробки, бумаги, шахматной доски; c) овала — яйца, зеркала, мячи;
5)
5 вещей, которыми ты действительно восхищаешься: жизнестойкость в людях, добрые поступки, художественное творчество, научные открытия, красота природы.

tasks.condition:
Write three questions. You want to know:
Напиши 3 вопроса. Ты хочешь узнать:
a) where your friend lived when he was little;
b) what he / she is interested in now;
c) where he / she is going for his / her winter holidays.

Speak about:
Поговори о:
1) royal palaces in London;
2) royal parks in London;
3) King Henry VII;
4) Queen Elizabeth I;
5) Queen Victoria.

Choose a partner and make up a dialogue about presents you get and give. Mention:
Выбери партнера и сочини диалог о том, какие подарки ты получаешь и какие подарки ты даришь. Упомяни:
— when you get / give presents;
— what you usually get / give;
— who gives you presents;
— where you buy presents;
— for whom you buy / to whom you give your presents;
— what presents you can make yourself;
— what was the best / the most unusual / the biggest / the nicest present you have ever got;
— what present you'd like to get for Christmas.

Put the lines in the limerick in the right order.
Поставь строки лимерика в правильном порядке.
a) When she said, “Tick−a−tack!”;
b) Which grieved [ɡri:vd] that Old Lady of France;
c) Who taught little ducklings ['dʌklɪŋz] to dance;
d) They only said, “Quack”;
e) There was an Old Lady of France.

tasks.solution:
e) There was an Old Lady of France,
c) Who taught little ducklings to dance;
a) When she said, “Tick−a−tack!”;
d) They only said, “Quack”;
b) Which grieved that Old Lady of France.
Перевод:
e) Жила−была старая леди из Франции,
c) Которая учила маленьких утят танцевать;
а) Когда она сказала: «Тик−так!»;
d) Они только сказали: «Кряк»;
b) Что огорчало ту старую леди из Франции.
